<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
	<TargetFramework>netstandard2.1</TargetFramework>
	<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
	<RootNamespace>Light.Mediator</RootNamespace>
	<AssemblyName>Lightsoft.Mediator</AssemblyName>
	<Title>Lightsoft.Mediator</Title>
	<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
	<Authors>minhvu</Authors>
	<Description>Package containing Mediator implements.</Description>
	<Summary>Package containing Mediator implements.</Summary>
	<Version>1.3.0</Version>
	<PackageTags>lightframework;dotnet;aspnetcore</PackageTags>
	<PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
	<PackageReleaseNotes>
1.3.0:
- AddBehaviors now validates that an open-generic behavior type implements IPipelineBehavior&lt;,&gt; before registering, instead of failing later with a confusing MakeGenericType exception during DI resolution.
- AddMediatorFromAssemblies now throws ArgumentNullException for a null element in the assemblies array, instead of an unfriendly NullReferenceException.
- Publish no longer silently drops an earlier notification handler's failure when a later handler is cancelled (OperationCanceledException/TaskCanceledException) mid-loop; buffered failures and the cancellation are now combined into a single AggregateException. Cancellation with no prior failures still propagates unchanged.
- Send() no longer allocates a closure/delegate when no pipeline behaviors are registered, matching the documented zero-alloc fast path.
	</PackageReleaseNotes>
	<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
	<PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
	<EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
	<AllowedOutputExtensionsInPackageBuildOutputFolder>$(AllowedOutputExtensionsInPackageBuildOutputFolder);.pdb</AllowedOutputExtensionsInPackageBuildOutputFolder>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.*" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Mediator.Contracts\Mediator.Contracts.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
